
---

# Task Manager API Pro

A production-ready RESTful API for task management built with **Node.js**, **Express 5**, and **MongoDB**. It features a complete authentication system (JWT, Email Verification, Forgot/Reset Password) and an advanced task management module with **Soft Delete**, **Favorites**, **Archive**, and **Statistics**. The API is fully documented using **Swagger**.

---

# Features

* User registration with email verification
* JWT-based authentication
* Forgot password & password reset using secure temporary tokens
* Change password for authenticated users
* Logout and user profile endpoints
* User roles (`user` / `admin`)
* Full Task CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
* Soft Delete with Restore functionality
* Favorite and Archive tasks
* Task statistics
* Search, filtering, sorting, field selection, and pagination
* Request validation using **express-validator**
* Centralized error handling
* Interactive API documentation with Swagger
* Security and performance middlewares:

  * Helmet
  * CORS
  * Compression
  * Morgan Logging

---

# Tech Stack

| Category           | Technology                             |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| Runtime            | Node.js                                |
| Framework          | Express 5                              |
| Database           | MongoDB + Mongoose 9                   |
| Authentication     | JSON Web Token (jsonwebtoken) + bcrypt |
| Validation         | express-validator                      |
| Email Service      | Nodemailer                             |
| API Documentation  | swagger-jsdoc + swagger-ui-express     |
| Security & Logging | helmet, cors, compression, morgan      |

---

# Project Structure

```text
src/
├── app.js                     # Express application configuration
├── server.js                  # Server entry point (Database connection + listen)
├── config/
│   ├── env.js                 # Environment variables
│   ├── db.js                  # MongoDB connection
│   └── swagger.js             # Swagger configuration
├── constants/
│   └── roles.js               # User roles
├── routes/
│   ├── auth.route.js          # Authentication routes
│   └── task.route.js          # Task routes
├── controllers/
│   ├── auth.controller.js
│   └── task.controller.js
├── middlewares/
│   ├── protect.middleware.js       # JWT authentication
│   ├── authorize.middleware.js     # Role authorization
│   ├── validate.middleware.js      # Validation handler
│   ├── asyncHandler.middleware.js  # Async error wrapper
│   └── errorHandler.middleware.js  # Global error handler
├── services/
│   ├── email.service.js       # Email service
│   └── task.service.js        # Task business logic
├── models/
│   ├── user.model.js
│   └── task.model.js
├── validations/
│   └── auth.validator.js
└── utils/
    └── AppError.js            # Custom error class
```

---

# Requirements

* Node.js **18+**
* MongoDB (Local or Atlas)
* SMTP email account for:

  * Email Verification
  * Password Reset

---

# Installation

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run in development mode
npm run dev

# Run in production mode
npm start
```

---

# Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root and add the following variables:

```env
PORT=
APP_NAME=
MONGO_URL=
JWT_SECRET=
EMAIL_HOST=
EMAIL_PORT=
EMAIL_USER=
EMAIL_PASS=
EMAIL_FROM=
BASE_URL=
```

---

# API Documentation

After starting the server, open:

```text
http://localhost:<PORT>/api-docs
```

Swagger provides interactive API documentation where you can test all endpoints directly.

For protected endpoints, authorize using:

```text
Bearer <your_token>
```

---

# API Endpoints

## Authentication (`/api/auth`)

| Method | Endpoint                 | Description                      | Protected |
| ------ | ------------------------ | -------------------------------- | --------- |
| POST   | `/register`              | Register a new user              | ❌         |
| POST   | `/login`                 | User login                       | ❌         |
| POST   | `/logout`                | User logout                      | ✅         |
| GET    | `/verify-email/:token`   | Verify email address             | ❌         |
| POST   | `/forgot-password`       | Request password reset           | ❌         |
| PATCH  | `/reset-password/:token` | Reset password                   | ❌         |
| PATCH  | `/change/password`       | Change current password          | ✅         |
| GET    | `/profile`               | Get authenticated user's profile | ✅         |

---

## Tasks (`/api/tasks`)

| Method | Endpoint        | Description                                                                          | Protected |
| ------ | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------- |
| POST   | `/`             | Create a new task                                                                    | ✅         |
| GET    | `/`             | Get all tasks (supports pagination, filtering, search, sorting, and field selection) | ✅         |
| GET    | `/statistics`   | Get task statistics                                                                  | ✅         |
| GET    | `/favorites`    | Get favorite tasks                                                                   | ✅         |
| GET    | `/archive`      | Get archived tasks                                                                   | ✅         |
| GET    | `/:id`          | Get a single task                                                                    | ✅         |
| PATCH  | `/:id`          | Update a task                                                                        | ✅         |
| PATCH  | `/:id/restore`  | Restore a soft-deleted task                                                          | ✅         |
| PATCH  | `/:id/favorite` | Toggle favorite status                                                               | ✅         |
| PATCH  | `/:id/archive`  | Toggle archive status                                                                | ✅         |
| DELETE | `/:id`          | Soft delete a task                                                                   | ✅         |

> **Protected routes require the following header:**

```http
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

---

# Data Models

## User

```text
name
email
password (hashed using bcrypt)
role (user | admin)
isVerified
passwordResetToken
emailVerificationToken
```

## Task

```text
title
description
status (pending | in-progress | completed)
priority (low | medium | high)
dueDate
category
isFavorite
isArchived
isDeleted
user (reference to the task owner)
```

---

# Error Handling

All API errors follow a consistent response format:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "status": "Fail",
  "message": "..."
}
```

The API also automatically converts common Mongoose and JWT errors into clear, user-friendly responses, including:

* Invalid MongoDB ObjectId
* Duplicate email address
* Mongoose validation errors
* Invalid or expired JWT
* Authentication and authorization errors

